a_1 &= 1, \, \\
a_{n+1} & - a_n = \begin{cases} 
p_k = \text{"the next prime number after the previous difference $p_{k-1}$"} & \text{if $n < i$}, \\ 
q_i = \begin{pmatrix} 
p_j & 0 \\ 
0 & q_i 
\end{pmatrix} & \text{otherwise},
\end{cases}
\end{aligned} $$
where the prime indices (\( p_i \)) start from the fifth prime ($p_5 = 11$). Find \( b_{10} \).

